3. Restrictions. Separate written permission from the relevant rights holder is required for (a) commercial use, including commercial business/product R&D, paid structure services, consultancy/hosting, sale, rental or integration into a commercial product; (b) modification, adaptation, translation or derivative versions of package code, instructions or documentation, including AI-generated patches; or (c) redistribution, forwarding, mirrors, public uploads, repackaging, resale or sublicensing of the package or protected portions, including unchanged copies. Paying for ordinary equipment, computing or an AI tool does not alone make academic use commercial. Industry-commissioned, commercially collaborative or otherwise uncertain uses need separate permission.

4. Configuration and agents. Recipients may edit external machine profiles, inputs and job parameters and generate normal run files without altering the package. Authorized AI agents may read and invoke it for permitted work; this does not grant the provider independent training, reuse, modification or distribution rights. Do not upload it to a service requiring broader rights. Report defects and reproduction steps; obtain patches from the maintainer or separate authorization to modify.

5. Research outputs. Lawfully controlled input data and ordinary resulting CIFs, models, checkCIF reports and bilingual reports are not subject to the software redistribution ban merely because Cairystal was used. Users may edit, publish and share research outputs they are entitled to share in lawful academic work. This does not permit publishing the package source/instructions. Third-party, service, template and publication rights remain separate. Accurate version/software citation is requested; coauthorship is not a condition.

6. Third parties and earlier rights. Dependencies and data-related rights retain their own terms; this licence neither relicenses nor adds restrictions to them. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. It does not revoke prior lawful grants or override non-waivable legal rights. Hosting-platform terms may confer additional rights and cannot be overridden by this file.

7. Termination and disclaimer. To the extent permitted by law, breach terminates the grant; stop unauthorized use and remove software copies you have no right to retain, without destroying research data you lawfully own. The package is provided as is, without warranties of availability, accuracy or suitability. Liability is excluded only to the extent permitted by law; non-excludable liability is unaffected. Users remain responsible for scientific review.

The licence covers only material the licensor is entitled to license. It does not replace third-party terms or certify an exhaustive legal review.
